Public-domain corpus of the Lucius Fundamentum benchmark.

machado-memorias-posthumas.txt
  Machado de Assis, "Memorias Posthumas de Braz Cubas" (1881; author died 1908).
  Obtained from Project Gutenberg, ebook #54829, with their header and footer
  removed. Original spelling of the 1881 edition kept as published. Normalized
  to Unicode NFC, LF line endings; no other change.

The six files below are Brazilian official acts. Legislation, decrees and the
resolutions of a federal council are outside copyright by statute (Lei 9.610,
art. 8), which is what `public-domain-law` records in the manifest. They are
here because the literary text above contains no numbered article, no acronym
and no composite number, so it cannot tell a lexical search apart from a dense
one; these can.

Each was converted from its published form to plain text. What was changed is
listed per file, and nothing else was: no spelling was modernized, no article
was reordered, no passage was cut.

Two changes were made to all six, for the same reason the literary text above
carries them: this library measures positions in code points, and a corpus
whose bytes depend on who checked it out cannot anchor a position. Line
endings are LF, and the text is Unicode NFC. The second one was not free:
ldb-9394 and resolucao-cne-ceb-2 each carried one "a" written as a plus a
combining grave accent rather than as the single code point, inherited from
the published HTML, and every offset after it differed by one. Composing them
is the only change made to a letter anywhere in these files.

lei-15100.txt
  Lei n. 15.100, de 13 de janeiro de 2025 (use of personal electronic devices
  by students). From the Diario Oficial da Uniao of 14 January 2025, section 1,
  page 3. The PDF is the whole page, so the file also carries Lei Complementar
  212 (Propag) and Lei 15.101, which were published beside it. They are kept:
  a question about phones in school that retrieves an article about state debt
  is a precision failure worth being able to measure.
  Removed: the page number, the ISSN line and the digital-signature footer.

decreto-12385.txt
  Decreto n. 12.385, de 18 de fevereiro de 2025, which regulates Lei 15.100.
  From the Diario Oficial da Uniao of 19 February 2025, section 1, page 3.
  Removed: the "este conteudo nao substitui" footer. Repaired: ten places where
  the extractor glued the italic span `caput` to its neighbours (`art. 84,caput`
  became `art. 84, caput`), and one place where it glued two words across an
  italic span (`ofensason-line` became `ofensas on-line`).

resolucao-cne-ceb-2.txt
  Resolucao CNE/CEB n. 2, de 21 de marco de 2025, the operational guidelines on
  digital devices in schools. Thirteen pages.
  Removed: twelve page-number lines the pagination had placed inside sentences.

ldb-9394.txt
  Lei n. 9.394, de 20 de dezembro de 1996 (Lei de Diretrizes e Bases da Educacao
  Nacional), consolidated text as published by the Presidencia da Republica.
  The consolidated form keeps repealed articles in place, each marked
  "(Revogado pela Lei n. X)"; they are kept as published.
  Removed: runs of layout whitespace, 2,606 non-breaking spaces the HTML used
  to push the amendment notes to the right margin. Only runs were removed:
  eight single non-breaking spaces survive as published, and a reader counting
  them in this file will find those eight. No note was removed.

pne-13005.txt
  Lei n. 13.005, de 25 de junho de 2014 (Plano Nacional de Educacao), with the
  Annex of twenty goals and their numbered strategies.

decreto-11713.txt
  Decreto n. 11.713, de 26 de setembro de 2023, which creates the Estrategia
  Nacional de Escolas Conectadas. It cites strategies 7.15 and 7.20 of the
  Annex to Lei 13.005, which is in this directory. That is the only reference
  to a numbered strategy made from outside the PNE, which is why the test
  suite uses it: `7.15` occurs in exactly two chunks of the whole corpus, one
  in each document.

Cross-document citation, counted on the six acts with the editorial margin
removed (the margin carries amendment history, not citation): nine directed
edges, the heaviest being decreto-12385 -> lei-15100, thirteen times. It is a
connected graph, not a pile of unrelated files, which is the property a
retrieval benchmark needs and the reason these six were chosen together.

Do not take that on trust: `npm run bench:corpus` prints the graph from the
files in this directory, and the suite fails if this paragraph and those files
stop agreeing. Every number above the graph comes from the same command.
